---
# Copy this file to `.claude/iac-security-scan.local.md` in your project to turn
# the terraform-apply security gate ON. It is OFF until this file exists with a
# mode other than `off`. Keep it out of git (add `.claude/*.local.md` to
# .gitignore) -- it is a per-developer local switch, not shared policy.

# apply_gate: off | warn | ask | block
#   off   -- disabled (the default; same as no file at all)
#   warn  -- allow the apply but print a loud warning
#   ask   -- ask you to confirm before applying
#   block -- deny the apply until the finding is fixed or the gate is turned off
apply_gate: block

# Severity floor. Findings at or above this level gate the apply.
# critical | high | medium | low
apply_gate_severity: critical

# Hard cap on scan time (seconds). If the scan takes longer it TIMES OUT and the
# apply is ALLOWED (fail-open), never blocked.
apply_gate_timeout: 120
---

# iac-security-scan apply-gate

This project has the opt-in `terraform apply` security gate configured above.

Remember: the gate **fails open**. If Checkov is missing, the scan errors, or it
times out, your `terraform apply` proceeds -- the gate warns you loudly but will
never wedge a deploy because the scanner broke. To turn it off, set
`apply_gate: off` above (or export `IAC_SECURITY_SCAN_APPLY_GATE=off`).
